home=f'''<section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> QUADMANN GAMING</p><h1>Same passion.<br>A different<br><em>way to play.</em></h1><p>Gaming brought competition back into my life. With a mouth-operated QuadStick, I play with friends, chase wins, and get lost in great stories.</p><div class="actions">{button('Watch My Best Clips','/clips/')}{button('Meet QuadMann','/my-story/',True)}</div></div><div class="hero-art"><span class="orbit" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="hero-word" aria-hidden="true"><span>PLAY WITH</span><strong>STYLE!</strong></span>{pic('portrait','QuadMann smiling with his mouth-operated gaming controller','hero-person',True)}<div class="image-note"><span class="dot"></span> MY SETUP. MY GAME.</div></div></section>
<div class="game-strip" aria-label="Games I play"><span>IN THE ROTATION</span><b>CALL OF DUTY</b><b>HALO</b><b>FORTNITE</b><b>STAR WARS JEDI</b><b>HOGWARTS LEGACY</b></div>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PRESS PLAY</p><h2>A little friendly competition.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/clips/">Explore my clips <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="video-grid">{card(videos[0])}{card(videos[4])}{card(videos[3])}</div></section>
<section class="split feature"><div class="device-image">{pic('quadstick','Front view of a QuadStick with its mouthpiece and tubing')}<span class="photo-label">THE CONTROLLER BEHIND THE GAMEPLAY</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">HOW I PLAY</p><h2>A few sips.<br>A few puffs.<br><em>A whole lot of possibility.</em></h2><p>I use my mouth to move the joystick, sip and puff to activate commands, and my bottom lip to use the lip control. Every game gets a setup that works for me.</p>{button('See how the QuadStick works','/how-it-works/',True)}</div></section>
<section class="split story-teaser"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEYOND THE CONTROLLER</p><h2>Still me.<br>Still competitive.</h2><p>From cross country in Raleigh to finding my way back to competition through gaming, this is the story behind QuadMann.</p>{button('Read My Story','/my-story/',True)}</div><figure>{pic('arches','QuadMann visiting a natural sandstone arch in Utah')}<figcaption>A little adventure beyond the screen.</figcaption></figure></section>{cta()}'''

story_sections=[
 ('Growing Up in Raleigh',"I grew up in Raleigh, North Carolina, and sports were a big part of my life. Over the years, I played soccer and lacrosse, plus one season of football—which was enough for me to know it wasn’t my sport.\nIn high school, I focused mainly on cross country and track. During my senior year, my 5K times were around 17 minutes, and my personal best in the mile was about 4 minutes and 47 seconds. Our cross country team finished second at the state championship. We had hoped to win, so that finish was disappointing at the time, even though we had accomplished a lot together.\nI also competed in pole vault during my junior and senior years. Outside of sports, I earned my Eagle Scout rank during my senior year of high school.\nBeing active, working toward a goal, and competing alongside others were all big parts of who I was growing up.",'cross-country','Runners competing in a cross country race','Cross country days.'),
 ('The Summer Everything Changed',"When I was 18, during the summer between high school graduation and my freshman year of college, I sustained a spinal cord injury in a diving accident. I was on a mission trip on the island of Eleuthera in the Bahamas.\nI was flown to Jackson Memorial Hospital in Miami, where I underwent an 11-hour surgery for a C4–C5 spinal cord injury. After spending roughly one to two months in the ICU, I transferred to the Shepherd Center in Atlanta, Georgia. There, I continued rehabilitation until I was off the ventilator and strong enough to return home.",'bahamas-group','A group standing together by the ocean on the Bahamas trip','With the group in the Bahamas.'),
 ('Continuing My Education',"Once I was home, I continued my education through online and in-person classes at NC State, Wake Tech, and UNC. Eventually, I earned enough credits to transfer to the University of North Carolina full time, where I graduated with a degree in Management and Society and a minor in Philosophy.\nToday, I work in digital content, social media, and marketing for a healthcare practice. I’m also a licensed real estate agent with Cox Distinctive Properties LLC.",'graduation','QuadMann outside a UNC building decorated for graduation','Graduation at UNC.'),
 ('Finding Competition Again',"After my injury, one of the things I missed most was competing. As a quadriplegic who uses a sip-and-puff wheelchair, I struggled to find an activity where I could compete alongside my friends.\nThen I started using the QuadStick.\nIt has changed my life in a meaningful way. Gaming has given me a way to reconnect with the competitive side of myself and spend time doing something I love with my friends. I play games like Halo, Call of Duty, FIFA, and Fortnite, and I love the teamwork, the competition, and the moments we share.\nI’ve also discovered how much I enjoy story-driven games, including the Star Wars Jedi series and Hogwarts Legacy.\nQuadMann Gaming is where I share that part of my life: the games, the setup, the big plays, and the fun of getting to compete again.",'gaming-scene','QuadMann smiling with his controller against a colorful gaming backdrop','Back in the game.')
]
